#
# STRLEN - non-existent key returns 0, empty string returns 0,
# populated key returns byte count.
#
0
OK
0
OK
13
#
# GETRANGE - positive indices inclusive on both ends.
#
Hello
World
H
Hello, World!
#
# GETRANGE - negative indices count from the end.
#
World!
!
#
# GETRANGE - inverted range (start > end) returns empty string.
#

#
# SETRANGE - in-place overwrite in the middle of the string.
#
OK
13
Hello, Redis!
#
# SETRANGE - offset at 0 overwrites from the start.
#
OK
10
ABCD456789
#
# SETRANGE - offset past end of string pads with zero bytes
# (verified via STRLEN; raw GET would contain \0 which interacts
# badly with the MTR diff framing).
#
OK
12
12
#
# SETRANGE on a non-existent key creates it with leading zero bytes.
#
6
6
#
# Cleanup.
#
6
